<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 9 February, from 474 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">474 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,552 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Child emperor Leo II crowns his father Zeno co-emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Seven-year-old Leo II, sole emperor since his grandfather's death in January, crowned his father Zeno as co-ruler. Leo died that November, leaving Zeno to rule alone.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohemia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1003 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,023 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Boleslaus III is restored in Bohemia with Polish armed support</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Boleslaus III the Red regained power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> with armed support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and his brothers fled again to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He soon undermined his position by ordering a massacre of the Vršovci nobles.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1234">1234 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">792 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caizhou falls to the Mongols and the Song, ending the Jin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mongol and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> forces took Caizhou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, under siege since December 1233. The Jin emperor Aizong had killed himself, and his short-lived successor died in the street fighting, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-caizhou">Siege of Caizhou</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1540">1540 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">486 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earliest recorded race is run at Chester</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Shrove Tuesday race on the Roodee at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> is the first recorded at what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s oldest racecourse still in use. It replaced a violent football match as the city's holiday sport.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament declares Massachusetts in rebellion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-westminster">Houses of Parliament</a> declared Massachusetts in a state of rebellion and asked the King to enforce the law. Fighting broke out at Lexington and Concord two months later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jefferson Davis elected provisional President of the Confederacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in Montgomery, the Confederate provisional Congress chose Davis, a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> senator and US Secretary of War. He led the Confederacy throughout the Civil War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph McCarthy claims to have a list of communists in the State Department</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at Wheeling, West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a> senator said he held a list of 205 communists in the State <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. The charge launched years of anti-communist investigations.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet R-7 becomes the first operational ICBM</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The R-7 Semyorka, the rocket that had launched Sputnik, entered service as the world's first intercontinental ballistic missile. Its descendants still launch Soyuz spacecraft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Beatles appear on 'The Ed Sullivan Show'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An estimated 73 million Americans watched the Beatles' first live US television appearance. The broadcast launched the 'British Invasion' of American popular music.</p></div></li></ol>
