<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 9 February <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sayf-al-dawla"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Sayf al-Dawla</span><span class="tp">916–967</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bernard-i-duke-of-saxony"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bernard-i-duke-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bernard I, Duke of Saxony</span><span class="tp">d. 1011</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-jin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-taizong-of-jin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Taizong of Jin</span><span class="tp">1075–1135</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/minamoto-no-yoritomo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Minamoto no Yoritomo</span><span class="tp">1147–1199</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick III of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1609–1670</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/miklos-horthy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Miklós Horthy</span><span class="tp">1868–1957</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
